            "promptText": "# Journey storyboard: First open of the keeper · flow-09\nid: flow-09 · platforms: ios/android/web · type: storyboard · artboards: 13\n\nUse the Pantopus house style pasted above and the Foundations components, by exact name. This project is a journey storyboard.\n\nTYPE: NEW (storyboard). Every screen in this journey was already designed in its own project. Do not redesign any screen. Place each attached export as a frame at 50% scale, connect the frames, and add callouts. Redraw a frame only where the REDRAW list says so. A redraw copies the named source artboard exactly (same components, same layout, same type) and changes only the deltas listed. Frame numbers F01 to F09 are the happy path. B1 to B10 are the failure branches. Print the frame number, the platform, the surface id and state, and the date and time above every frame (for example \"F02 · iOS · f1-today-tab · saved place with keeper invitation · Wed 21 Oct, 7:40 AM\").\nARTBOARD NAMES: storyboard artboards put \"storyboard\" in the platform slot (\"flow-09 · storyboard · 01-before-the-tap-lane · light\"), and the last artboard is \"flow-09 · Notes\". This overrides the house-style pattern \"<surface-id> · <platform> · <NN-state> · <theme>\".\nFACTCOUNT NAMES: use the component-contract variant names: \"keeper strip\", \"place file header\" and \"T1 (only Place and Dates can appear)\". Where an export labels them \"V2\" or \"V3\", print the contract name with the export label in brackets.\n\nATTACH (exported artboards, by exact name)\nHappy path:\n- f1-today-tab · ios · 02-saved-place-quiet · light (source for R1 and R2)\n- f5-today-calendar-strip · ios · 14-saved-outside-window · light (the 14-day card inside R1)\n- f5-today-calendar-strip · ios · 03-saved-place-unconfirmed · light (the 14-day card inside R2)\n- f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 06-saved-place-unconfirmed · light (the PickupCard inside R2)\n- f11-keeper-strip · ios · 07-invitation · light (source for the invitation row in R1 and R2)\n- f11-keeper-naming · ios · 02-default · light (source for R3)\n- f11-keeper-naming · ios · 09-saved-place · light (F04)\n- f11-keeper-naming · ios · 05-saving · light (source for R4)\n- f11-keeper-naming · ios · 07-named-landing · light (source for R5)\n- f11-keeper-strip · ios · 13-saved-place · light (source for R5)\n- x-place-file · ios · 02-saved-place-first-week · light (source for R6 and R10)\n- f11-keeper-strip · ios · 05-calm · light (source for R7)\n- f11-keeper-strip · ios · 06-unavailable · light (source for R8)\nFailure branches:\n- f11-keeper-naming · ios · 08-skipped-landing · light; f11-keeper-strip · ios · 08-skipped · light; f11-keeper-naming · ios · 14-reentry · light (B1, with R9, R10 and R13)\n- f11-keeper-naming · ios · 06-save-error · light; f11-keeper-naming · ios · 13-offline · light (B3, B4, with R13)\n- f11-keeper-strip · ios · 14-alert-suppressed · light; f1-today-tab · ios · 04-alert-pinned · light (B5, with R12)\n- f11-keeper-strip · ios · 16-offline · light (B6, with R13)\n- f11-keeper-strip · ios · 09-menu-open · light; f11-keeper-strip · ios · 10-hide-choice · light; f11-keeper-strip · ios · 11-removed-undo · light (B7, with R13)\n- f1-claim-receipt · ios · 03-only-you-so-far-pending · light; f1-today-tab · ios · 13-after-claim · light (B8, with R14 and R16)\n- f11-keeper-strip · ios · 12-member-view · light; f11-keeper-naming · ios · 10-member-read-only · light (B9)\nPlatform twins (these exports show HOME A; see the captions on artboard 09):\n- f11-keeper-naming · android · 15-otter-picked · light; f11-keeper-naming · web-1440 · 16-otter-picked · light; f11-keeper-naming · web-390 · 17-otter-picked · light\n- f11-keeper-strip · android · 18-busy-dense · light; f11-keeper-strip · web-1440 · 19-busy-dense · light; f11-keeper-strip · web-390 · 20-busy-dense · light\nAccessibility references:\n- f11-keeper-strip · ios · 21-ax5 · light; f11-keeper-strip · ios · 22-greyscale · light; f11-keeper-strip · ios · 23-pose-sheet · light; f11-keeper-naming · ios · 18-ax5 · light; f11-keeper-naming · ios · 19-greyscale · light\n\nREDRAW (no export exists for this exact moment; redraw faithfully from the source named)\n- R1 = F01. Source: f1-today-tab · ios · 02-saved-place-quiet. Deltas: Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM. No FirstWeekRow: Jordan saved on Sat 10 Oct, so his first 7 days ran Sat 10 to Fri 16 Oct. Location row \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\" · ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\" · \"Updated 4m ago\". Slot 3 is the QuietDayReceipt, because nothing is due tomorrow at PLACE B: \"Nothing needs your attention today\" with \"Checked 6:00 PM · weather · air · alerts · your calendar\". The property-tax signal below the receipt stays as the source draws it (\"Pay property tax, 2nd half\" · \"in 14 days · due Mon 2 Nov\"). Slot 4 is the 14-day card from f5-today-calendar-strip · ios · 14-saved-outside-window (window Mon 19 Oct to Sun 1 Nov): \"Next 14 days: 4 items\", the status line \"Saved · Lease ends Wed 31 Mar 2027 is in your place file · See it\", hollow Thursday rows (\"in 3 days · Thu 22 Oct\", \"in 10 days · Thu 29 Oct\"), the Mon 26 Oct statewide bar, and Jordan's \"Renters insurance renews\" · \"in 11 days · Fri 30 Oct\" · \"Repeats yearly\" with the you-added tick. Slot 4b is the keeper invitation row from f11-keeper-strip · ios · 07-invitation, with the PLACE B title: an outline silhouette in text.secondary, \"Give this place a keeper\", and a 44pt outlined \"Skip\". Slots 5 onward follow the source.\n- R2 = F02. Source: R1. Deltas: Wed 21 Oct, 7:40 AM. Slot 3 is now the PickupCard from f4-today-pickup-card · ios · 06-saved-place-unconfirmed: headline \"Garbage tomorrow\", the hollow mark with \"City schedule, not yet confirmed\", \"Recycling: Not set\", the buttons \"Yes, Thursday is right\" and \"Change pickup day\", and the footer \"Only you will see this. No night-before reminder until you confirm your day.\" The property-tax signal re-dates to \"in 12 days · due Mon 2 Nov\". The 14-day card is f5-today-calendar-strip · ios · 03-saved-place-unconfirmed, re-dated to Wed 21 Oct; its window runs Wed 21 Oct to Tue 3 Nov, so the week-two label above cell 8 reads \"Wed 28\". Its rows, in date order, are exactly:\n  - \"Pickup day\" · \"Which bins go out isn't set yet\" · \"Tomorrow · Thu 22 Oct\" · hollow, with the \"Set your pickup day\" button;\n  - the Mon 26 Oct statewide voter bar, \"in 5 days · must arrive by Mon 26 Oct\";\n  - \"Pickup day\" · \"in 8 days · Thu 29 Oct\" · hollow;\n  - \"Renters insurance renews\" · \"in 9 days · Fri 30 Oct\" · \"Repeats yearly\" · you-added tick;\n  - \"Pay property tax, 2nd half\" · \"in 12 days · due Mon 2 Nov\" (county bar, as R9, R11 and R12 draw it);\n  - the Tue 3 Nov statewide bar (in-person voting until 8:00 PM) · \"in 13 days\".\n  Summary \"Next 14 days: 6 items\". No status line (the lease status line in R1 was a one-visit polite status). The invitation row is unchanged at 4b, and the tap target is marked with a touch dot.\n- R3 = F03. Source: f11-keeper-naming · ios · 02-default, over R2 behind the scrim. PLACE B deltas: title \"Give this place a keeper\"; the scope block is the single line \"Only you will see this.\" Remove the HOME A lines \"Everyone in this household will see this.\" and \"What it says is based on what each person can see.\" The body lines, the six tiles (Octopus: Otto · River otter: Ollie · Great blue heron: Stilt · Red fox: Pepper · Raccoon: Bandit · Douglas squirrel: Doug), the empty \"Keeper's name\" field, the pinned equal buttons \"Name the keeper\" (disabled) and \"Skip\", and the caption \"Pick an animal first\" all follow the source.\n- R4 = F05. Source: f11-keeper-naming · ios · 05-saving, with F04's PLACE B content: Red fox selected, \"Pepper\", \"6 / 24\". The scope block is the single line \"Only you will see this.\"; remove the second HOME A line. The primary shows \"Saving…\". Tiles, field and Skip are disabled.\n- R5 = F06. Source: f11-keeper-strip · ios · 13-saved-place, with the landing caption from f11-keeper-naming · ios · 07-named-landing. Deltas: Wed 21 Oct, 7:41 AM (the export is dated Wed 21 Oct, 6:10 PM), the host is R2. The strip reads \"Pepper\" with the mood word \"On it\" and a chevron. The mood line is \"Garbage tomorrow.\" followed by a wordless hollow ProvenanceMark of at least 12pt. FactCount, keeper strip variant under the T1 rule [export label \"V3\"], reads \"5 on file\" with the pips Place · Dates only (the export says \"7 on file\" and \"Pickup tomorrow.\"; both change here). The on-it pose is the Red fox, upright and looking toward the line. The caption \"Pepper is on Today now.\" sits under the strip. The PickupCard above still carries \"City schedule, not yet confirmed\" once.\n- R6 = F07. Source: x-place-file · ios · 02-saved-place-first-week. Deltas: Wed 21 Oct, 7:42 AM. There is no \"Set up your place\" block, because the first week ended on Fri 16 Oct (the export dates the save Sat 17 Oct). The header reads \"Your place file\", \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\", \"Camas, WA 98607\", ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\", and FactCount, place file header variant under the T1 rule, \"5 on file\" with the pips Place · Dates, plus the legend line. Directly under the year band card, the standalone \"Next for this place\" FactRow reads \"Set your pickup day\" with the filled button \"Set pickup day\" and \"Not now · Skip\" (the first undone first-week step). The county lane reads \"County dates aren't available for a saved place\". The Place section holds the address, \"Pickup day · Thursday · how often: Not set\" with the hollow mark and \"City of Camas · pickup Thursdays · not yet confirmed\", the Thanksgiving line as the export draws it, \"Moved in · Not set · Add\", and the row \"Keeper · Pepper · Red fox\". Dates holds the voter row (\"in 5 days · must arrive by Mon 26 Oct\"), then \"Renters insurance renews · in 9 days · Fri 30 Oct\", \"Tell your landlord in writing by Mon 1 Mar 2027 · in 4 months · Mon 1 Mar 2027\" and \"Lease ends · in 5 months · Wed 31 Mar 2027\" (the place file's own month form for far dates), each with the you-added tick, and \"More you can add (2)\" (Warranty ends, HOA dues). The other categories show the single grey row \"Money, people and proof · Not here — this is a saved place · Claim this address first\", with no button and no count. The count block has a focus ring, showing where focus lands.\n- R7 = F08. Source: f11-keeper-strip · ios · 05-calm (exported for Wed 21 Oct at HOME A). Deltas: Sat 31 Oct, 8:00 AM, at PLACE B, with R1's location row and ScopeChip; the keeper is Pepper. The strip reads \"Pepper · Calm\" with the Red fox in the settled sitting pose and \"5 on file\" (Place · Dates). The mood line is the saved-place proposal \"Nothing of yours due in the next 7 days.\" (invented; list on Notes). Beside the strip, outside the frame, the export string \"No bills or dates due in the next 7 days.\" is drawn crossed out with the caption \"export string: claims no dates while property tax (Mon 2 Nov) is on screen below\", and an \"Honesty · MISMATCH\" tag. Slot 3 is the QuietDayReceipt with every CheckItem ticked: \"Nothing needs your attention today\" and \"Checked 7:45 AM · weather · air · alerts · your calendar\". Below it, the property-tax signal reads \"in 2 days · due Mon 2 Nov\" (shown, not a PLACE B mood input). There is no invitation anywhere.\n- R8 = F09. Source: f11-keeper-strip · ios · 06-unavailable (exported at HOME A with no date). Deltas: Mon 2 Nov, 7:40 AM, at PLACE B, with R1's location row and ScopeChip. Neutral front-facing outline pose, no mood word, \"Couldn't check what's due. Your dates didn't load.\" and \"Retry\". The QuietDayReceipt shows the failed CheckItem \"your calendar · Couldn't check · Retry\" and no \"Nothing needs your attention today\" heading. No row is drawn from the failed load. Inset beside it, labelled \"after Retry succeeds\": \"Pepper · Calm\" / \"Nothing of yours due in the next 7 days.\", with the property-tax signal \"Today · due Mon 2 Nov\" visible below it and the crossed-out export string \"No bills or dates due in the next 7 days.\" beside the inset with the same \"Honesty · MISMATCH\" tag.\n- R9 = B1's next Today. Source: R2. Deltas: Fri 23 Oct, 7:30 AM (the day after the Thursday pickup). No invitation and no empty gap at 4b. Slot 3 is the QuietDayReceipt (\"Nothing needs your attention today\", \"Checked 7:15 AM · weather · air · alerts · your calendar\"). The property-tax signal reads \"in 10 days · due Mon 2 Nov\". The 14-day card covers Fri 23 Oct to Thu 5 Nov: the Mon 26 Oct statewide bar (\"in 3 days\"), \"in 6 days · Thu 29 Oct\" (hollow), \"Renters insurance renews\" · \"in 7 days · Fri 30 Oct\" (tick), \"Pay property tax, 2nd half\" · \"in 10 days · due Mon 2 Nov\", the Tue 3 Nov statewide bar (\"in 11 days\"), and \"in 13 days · Thu 5 Nov\" (hollow). Summary \"Next 14 days: 6 items\". Caption \"never asks again\".\n- R10 = B1's way back in the place file. Source: R6. Deltas: the \"Keeper · Pepper · Red fox\" row is replaced by \"Give this place a keeper · Add\"; the date is Fri 23 Oct, 7:31 AM, so the dated rows read \"in 7 days · Fri 30 Oct\", \"in 4 months · Mon 1 Mar 2027\" and \"in 5 months · Wed 31 Mar 2027\", and the voter row reads \"in 3 days\". Then f11-keeper-naming · ios · 14-reentry with the title \"Give this place a keeper\", the single scope line \"Only you will see this.\" and no Skip. After Save, the row reads \"Keeper · Pepper · Red fox\". The same R10 place file, after a Remove in B7, shows the \"Give this place a keeper · Add\" row.\n- R11 = B2's Today. Source: R1. Deltas: Sun 1 Nov, 8:00 AM. No invitation and no gap at 4b (the 14-day invitation window, Sat 17 to Fri 30 Oct, has ended), no Undo, no message. Slot 3 is the QuietDayReceipt (\"Checked 7:45 AM · weather · air · alerts · your calendar\"), with the property-tax signal below it reading \"Tomorrow · due Mon 2 Nov\". The 14-day card covers Sun 1 Nov to Sat 14 Nov: \"Pay property tax, 2nd half\" · \"Tomorrow · due Mon 2 Nov\", the Tue 3 Nov statewide bar (\"in 2 days\"), \"in 4 days · Thu 5 Nov\" (hollow) and \"in 11 days · Thu 12 Nov\" (hollow). Summary \"Next 14 days: 4 items\". Renters insurance has passed and is not shown. No status line.\n- R12 = B5. Sources: f1-today-tab · ios · 04-alert-pinned and f11-keeper-strip · ios · 14-alert-suppressed (both HOME A). Deltas: Tue 27 Oct, 4:10 PM (illustrative), at PLACE B: location row \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\" · ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\"; the pinned AqiBand alert \"AQI 118 · Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups\", crossed at 4:00 PM, owns the top of the screen; no PickupCard (nothing is collected tomorrow at PLACE B); the keeper slot collapses to zero height, and no avatar or mood appears anywhere. The 14-day card covers Tue 27 Oct to Mon 9 Nov: \"in 2 days · Thu 29 Oct\" (hollow), \"Renters insurance renews\" · \"in 3 days · Fri 30 Oct\" (tick), \"Pay property tax, 2nd half\" · \"in 6 days · due Mon 2 Nov\", the Tue 3 Nov statewide bar (\"in 7 days\") and \"in 9 days · Thu 5 Nov\" (hollow). Summary \"Next 14 days: 5 items\".\n- R13 = the PLACE B swaps for B1, B3, B4, B6 and B7. Apply these to the named HOME A exports and change nothing else.\n  Host Today, by branch:\n  - B1 (Skip landing): the host is R2 (Wed 21 Oct, 7:40 AM) with the invitation row removed and slot 4b at zero height. No keeper, no avatar and no mood line anywhere.\n  - B3 (save error) and B4 (offline at naming): the host is R2 (Wed 21 Oct, 7:40 AM to 7:41 AM) behind the scrim, with the invitation row still at 4b. No keeper exists yet.\n  - B6 (offline on Today) and B7 (hide or remove): the host is R5 (Wed 21 Oct, 7:41 AM) with its location row and ScopeChip; the mood line is \"Garbage tomorrow.\" with the wordless hollow mark; FactCount reads \"5 on file\" (Place · Dates).\n  Sheet swaps (B1, B3, B4): the sheet title reads \"Give this place a keeper\"; the scope block is the single line \"Only you will see this.\"; where the export shows a selected tile and a filled field (B3), the selected tile is Red fox and the field reads \"Pepper\" and \"6 / 24\"; B4's sheet keeps the export's selection state with the PLACE B tile names.\n  Keeper swaps (B6, B7 only, where a keeper exists): the keeper's name reads \"Pepper\"; the offline freshness reads \"On it · as of 7:41 AM\"; the hide options read \"Hide for 7 days · until Wed 28 Oct\" and \"Hide for 31 days · until Sat 21 Nov\", with \"Keeper hidden until Wed 28 Oct · Undo\"; the remove line reads \"Keeper removed · Undo\" (never the household form \"Ollie removed for everyone in this household · Undo\").\n- R14 = B8's claim receipt. Source: f1-claim-receipt · ios · 03-only-you-so-far-pending (Maya's HOME A receipt). Deltas, all logged against f1-claim-receipt: Wed 28 Oct, 6:10 PM (illustrative; flow-06 owns the real date); the caption \"Address confirmed by postcard · Wed 28 Oct\"; the address 1107 NE Birchfield Ct; the summary \"Your pickup day, 2 dates and Pepper came with you.\"; the manifest rows: \"Pickup day · Thursday · how often: Not set\" with the hollow mark (not confirmed) and the caption \"Everyone in this household will see this.\" (scope pair Only you → household); \"Renters insurance renews · in 2 days · Fri 30 Oct\" (scope pair Only you → household, pending); \"Lease ends · in 154 days · Wed 31 Mar 2027\" (the receipt's own day-count form) with the caption \"Notice due Mon 1 Mar 2027\" (scope pair Only you → household, pending; the notice deadline rides on its lease row, as the export's rule says, so it is not a separate row); \"Pepper (your keeper) · Red fox\" with the caption \"Everyone in this household will see this.\" (scope pair Only you → household). The consent question reads \"Share the 2 dates you entered with people who join this household?\". The count line reads \"5 on file\" with the pips Place · Dates, by the x-place-file rule (the export says \"11 on file\"). Remove Maya's Tuesday, warranty, Ollie and her Feb reminder caption. Callouts: \"The receipt says 2 dates and the place file counts 3, because the notice deadline is a caption here and its own row there.\" and \"The pickup-day and keeper rows change scope with no choice offered; see the consent check.\"\n- R15 = B10's three specimens. Sources: (a) R1 with f11-keeper-naming · ios · 02-default (R3's content) presented over it without a tap; (b) the iOS lock screen with one notification, title \"Pepper misses you\", body \"Birchfield Ct\", drawn in PushCopy styling; (c) R5 with a streak chip \"3-day streak\" beside the name and the mood line replaced by \"Pepper knows 5 things\". All three strings are forbidden and exist only inside the crossed-out specimens.\n- R16 = B8's claimed Today. Source: f1-today-tab · ios · 13-after-claim (in that project slot 4b has zero height, and the export dates Jordan's save Sat 17 Oct). Deltas: Wed 28 Oct, 6:10 PM (illustrative); the location row \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\" with ScopeChip \"Your household\"; the LandingBannerSlot notice \"Birchfield Ct is now your home · See what moved\" kept in the pinned slot; the renters-insurance row keeps its \"Only you\" SourceCaption ending, as the export draws it. Slot 4b now holds the keeper strip: \"Pepper\" with the household mood for that evening, \"Busy\" / \"3 things due in the next 7 days.\" (Thu 29 Oct pickup, counted the day before; renters insurance Fri 30 Oct; property tax Mon 2 Nov, now a mood input at a claimed home), the Red fox in the holding-papers pose, and FactCount, keeper strip variant [export label \"V2\"], \"5 on file\" with the pips Place · Dates. The PickupCard in slot 3 reads \"Garbage tomorrow\" with its hollow mark. Every other section follows the export.\n\nPERSONA & SITUATION\n- Jordan Lee, 36, at PLACE B (1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas, WA 98607, \"Saved place · Only you\", tier T1). He moved from Portland, OR on Fri 9 Oct and saved the place on Sat 10 Oct. It is not claimed. The City of Camas says his pickup weekday is Thursday. The frequency is Not set, so every pickup mark is hollow. He has never turned notifications on.\n- On Sun 11 Oct he added the small Pantopus widget (\"Birchfield Ct\") to his home screen (invented date; list on Notes). He opens Pantopus from the app icon, not from the widget, on every frame here.\n- His first value moment was a saved date: \"Renters insurance renews\" on Fri 30 Oct, added on Tue 13 Oct (invented; list on Notes). With the address saved, the widget on and a date added inside his first 7 days (Sat 10 to Fri 16 Oct), Jordan became an activated user under design doc §1 and §5 on Tue 13 Oct, when the last criterion was met, with notifications still off. On Mon 19 Oct at 6:08 PM he also saved \"Lease ends\" on Wed 31 Mar 2027 with 30 days' notice, which added the notice deadline, Mon 1 Mar 2027.\n- One definition of the first week: Sat 10 to Fri 16 Oct. It is both the §5 activation window and the FirstWeekRow's life, so the FirstWeekRow is gone from Sat 17 Oct.\n- What is on file, under the x-place-file count rule: Place 2 (the address and the hollow Thursday seed) and Dates 3 (renters insurance, lease ends, notice deadline). That makes \"5 on file\". The keeper and the widget are not counted, and county and state rules are shown but not counted.\n- Mood at PLACE B: the keeper's mood comes from Jordan's own rows plus the seeded pickup. Seeded property tax (a county signal for property owners) and seeded civic rows are shown on Today but are not PLACE B mood inputs (a decision this storyboard states; logged as a MISMATCH). Because those rows stay visible, the saved-place Calm line is scoped to Jordan's own items (proposal \"Nothing of yours due in the next 7 days.\").\n- The invitation window: the invitation appears only after the FirstWeekRow has gone, so it was first eligible on Sat 17 Oct and lasts at most 14 days, through Fri 30 Oct. Jordan's first visit with it was Sun 18 Oct (not drawn). F01 is his second visit with the invitation, and F02 is his third.\n- TODAY is Mon 19 Oct 2026, 6:10 PM. Time moves forward to Wed 21 Oct, 7:40 AM (checking whether the bins go out tonight before work), to Sat 31 Oct, 8:00 AM, and to Mon 2 Nov, 7:40 AM.\n\nGOAL: Answer \"what's due?\" first. Let Jordan give the place a face in one or two taps, or skip it for good at no cost.\n\n§5 METRIC THIS JOURNEY MOVES\n- Week-four return: does the face change return among activated users? Jordan is activated (address saved Sat 10 Oct, widget Sun 11 Oct, a date Tue 13 Oct), so he is in the cohort. His account started Sat 10 Oct, so his week 4 runs Sat 31 Oct to Fri 6 Nov. F08 and F09 fall inside it. Annotate F01, F02, F08 and F09 with session_open{trigger:'organic'}. The keeper never creates a push trigger.\n- Also measured by the removal rate (B7) and the skip rate (B1). §5 defines no keeper event, so list the proposed FunnelEvent types keeper_named, keeper_skipped and keeper_removed on Notes as an open instrumentation item.\n- Must not affect Honesty: the mood line never presents the unconfirmed Thursday as confirmed (F06 carries the hollow mark), Calm never hides a due item it counts, and a Calm line never claims \"no dates\" while a date is on screen (F08, F09 inset). Put a small \"Honesty\" tag on those callouts.\n\nTHE HAPPY PATH\nEach step lists the platform, the surface and state, what Jordan does, what the screen shows, what is carried to the next step, and the MOMENT OF TRUTH callout for the margin lane.\n\nF01 · iOS · f1-today-tab · saved place, keeper slot with invitation (R1) · Mon 19 Oct, 6:10 PM\n- Does: reads the quiet receipt and the 14-day card, sees the lease status line, ignores the invitation and leaves.\n- Shows: \"Nothing needs your attention today\", the receipt, the property-tax heads-up, \"Next 14 days: 4 items\", and the invitation row \"Give this place a keeper\" with \"Skip\".\n- Carries forward: nothing. The invitation stays; ignoring it is not a decline.\n- MOMENT OF TRUTH: Nothing opens on its own, on the second open or any other. Today works fully while the invitation is ignored.\n\nTIME GAP: \"Two days later · Wed 21 Oct, 7:40 AM\".\n\nF02 · iOS · f1-today-tab · pickup tomorrow, invitation (R2) · Wed 21 Oct, 7:40 AM\n- Does: reads \"Garbage tomorrow\" first, then taps the invitation row (his third visit with it).\n- Shows: the PickupCard with its hollow mark and \"City schedule, not yet confirmed\"; the 14-day card (\"Next 14 days: 6 items\"); the invitation row at 4b, between the 14-day card and the weather.\n- Carries forward: the place id (PLACE B), the tier (T1, saved place) and the entry point (Today invitation).\n- MOMENT OF TRUTH: The invitation is a quiet row, never a badge, dot or modal. It appears only after a value moment and after the first week, for at most 14 days. The outline silhouette meets 3:1.\n\nF03 · iOS · f11-keeper-naming · default, PLACE B (R3) · 7:40 AM\n- Does: reads the sheet.\n- Shows: \"Give this place a keeper\", \"A small animal on Today that sums up what's due here.\", \"You can rename or remove it any time.\", six tiles, \"Keeper's name\", the single scope line \"Only you will see this.\", and the equal pinned buttons \"Name the keeper\" and \"Skip\" with \"Pick an animal first\".\n- Carries forward: the scope (Only you).\n- MOMENT OF TRUTH: Skip is a real, neutral button of the same size and weight, visible without scrolling. There are no pronouns, traits or quiz.\n\nF04 · iOS · f11-keeper-naming · 09-saved-place · 7:40 AM\n- Does: taps Red fox.\n- Shows: the Red fox tile selected (filled radio dot, bold label, 2px text.primary outline), the field filled with \"Pepper\", the counter \"6 / 24\", \"Only you will see this.\", and \"Name the keeper\" enabled.\n- Carries forward: species Red fox, name \"Pepper\" (not edited).\n- MOMENT OF TRUTH: One tap is enough. Selection does not look like the focus ring, and focus stays on the tile instead of jumping to the field.\n\nF05 · iOS · f11-keeper-naming · saving (R4) · 7:41 AM\n- Does: taps \"Name the keeper\".\n- Shows: \"Saving…\" on the primary, with the other controls disabled.\n- Carries forward: a keeper object for this saved place: name \"Pepper\", species Red fox, scope Only you.\n- MOMENT OF TRUTH: The save is announced as a status message. There is no confetti, badge or \"Level 1\". One light haptic tick when it succeeds.\n\nF06 · iOS · f11-keeper-strip · on it, saved place (R5) · Wed 21 Oct, 7:41 AM\n- Does: reads the strip, then taps \"5 on file\".\n- Shows: \"Pepper · On it\", \"Garbage tomorrow.\" with the wordless hollow mark, FactCount \"5 on file\" (Place · Dates), and the caption \"Pepper is on Today now.\".\n- Carries forward: the count 5 and its categories.\n- MOMENT OF TRUTH (Honesty): The mood comes only from records: the Thursday pickup, counted on the day before, and Jordan's own dates. The pose helps and is never distressed. There is no denominator and no outline for categories he cannot reach at T1. Under Reduce Motion the pose is static.\n\nF07 · iOS · x-place-file · T1 saved place (R6) · 7:42 AM\n- Does: reads the header count and the Keeper row, then goes Back.\n- Shows: \"5 on file\" with Place · Dates, the \"Set your pickup day\" Next row, the hollow Thursday row, \"Keeper · Pepper · Red fox\", the three dated rows, and the grey \"Money, people and proof\" row.\n- Carries forward: nothing. Back returns to Today with focus on the count.\n- MOMENT OF TRUTH: The keeper's count and the place file's count are the same number, computed by the same rule.\n\nTIME GAP: \"Ten days later · Sat 31 Oct, 8:00 AM\".\n\nF08 · iOS · f11-keeper-strip · calm, saved place (R7) · Sat 31 Oct, 8:00 AM\n- Does: glances at Today and leaves.\n- Shows: \"Pepper · Calm\" / \"Nothing of yours due in the next 7 days.\" (proposal), with the crossed-out export string beside the frame; the fully ticked receipt; and the property-tax heads-up below it.\n- Carries forward: nothing.\n- Margin note on the window, Sat 31 Oct to Fri 6 Nov: \"Renters insurance passed on Fri 30 Oct. The Thu 5 Nov pickup counts only on Wed 4 Nov. County and state rules (property tax Mon 2 Nov, in-person voting Tue 3 Nov) are shown but excluded from mood and not counted. Voter registration is always excluded from mood.\"\n- Callout, tagged \"Honesty · MISMATCH\": \"The export Calm line 'No bills or dates due in the next 7 days.' would sit directly above 'Pay property tax, 2nd half · in 2 days · due Mon 2 Nov', and the window also holds the Tue 3 Nov voting day. The line claims no dates while a date is on screen. The storyboard draws a line scoped to Jordan's own items as the proposal; the export string is shown crossed out. Logged for f11-keeper-strip.\"\n- MOMENT OF TRUTH (Honesty): Calm appears only when the keeper's own checks all succeeded and none of its own inputs is due in the window, and its words claim only what the keeper checked.\n\nTIME GAP: \"Two days later · Mon 2 Nov, 7:40 AM\".\n\nF09 · iOS · f11-keeper-strip · unavailable, saved place (R8) · Mon 2 Nov, 7:40 AM\n- Does: taps \"Retry\".\n- Shows: the neutral outline pose, no mood word, \"Couldn't check what's due. Your dates didn't load.\", \"Retry\", and a failed CheckItem with no all-clear heading. The inset shows Calm after the retry succeeds, with the proposed line \"Nothing of yours due in the next 7 days.\" above property tax due today (still not a PLACE B mood input), and the crossed-out export string beside it with the same Honesty MISMATCH tag.\n- Carries forward: nothing. The journey ends here.\n- MOMENT OF TRUTH: Unavailable can never be mistaken for Calm. It names what failed and offers Retry.\n\nLAYOUT\n- Artboards are 2400 wide, on surface.app, and at least 1500 tall. Height grows in 520px rows to fit the content: never scale a storyboard frame below 50%, and never overlap frames, callouts or caption strips. Navigation thumbnails (branch start and rejoin thumbnails, and the focus-path strip on artboard 12) are 25% and carry the small label \"thumbnail\". Each artboard carries its visible name label above it.\n- Artboards 01–04 (happy path) have no failure lane. Their bands, top to bottom:\n  (1) the margin lane: moment-of-truth callouts, each tied by a thin text.secondary leader to its frame, headed \"MOMENT OF TRUTH · F06\";\n  (2) the happy-path lane: iOS frames at 50% (196x426), shown at full scroll length where the source export is full-length, with a bracket marking the first viewport. Android frames are 206x458, web-390 frames 195x422, and web-1440 frames 720x450. Leave 48px between frames.\n- Under each happy-path frame where a branch starts, draw a small caption tag naming the branch and its artboard: F01 \"Branches: B2 → artboard 05 · B10a → 08\"; F02 \"B1 → 05\"; F03 \"B1, B4 → 05\"; F05 \"B3 → 05\"; F06 \"B5, B6, B7 → 06 · B8 → 07 · B10b, B10c → 08\"; F07 \"B9 (HOME A) → 07\".\n- Artboards 05–08 (branches) hold one row per branch. Each row starts with a 25% thumbnail of its start frame, labelled \"thumbnail · from F06\" (or wherever it starts), then a dashed arrow labelled by the condition, then its frames at 50%, then either a solid arrow labelled \"rejoins at F06\" (or wherever it rejoins) with a 25% thumbnail of that frame, or the caption \"ends here\". The branch's moment-of-truth callouts sit above its row.\n- Arrows are 1.5px text.strong lines with a solid head. Each is labelled with its trigger in caption type: \"organic open\", \"reads, leaves\", \"tap Give this place a keeper\", \"tap Red fox\", \"tap Name the keeper\", \"sheet closes · pose settles\", \"tap 5 on file\", \"Back\", \"organic open\", \"tap Retry\".\n- Time jumps are a 96px gap with a vertical dashed rule and a label chip in surface.sunken: \"Two days later · Wed 21 Oct, 7:40 AM\", \"Ten days later · Sat 31 Oct, 8:00 AM\" and \"Two days later · Mon 2 Nov, 7:40 AM\".\n- On artboard 01, a thin timeline runs above the lane. It marks Sat 10 Oct (saved · first week starts), Sun 11 Oct (widget added), Tue 13 Oct (first date · activated), Fri 16 Oct (first week and activation window close), Sat 17 Oct (FirstWeekRow gone · invitation eligible), Sun 18 Oct (first visit with the invitation), Mon 19 Oct (F01), Wed 21 Oct (named), Fri 30 Oct (last day of the invitation window) and Sat 31 Oct to Fri 6 Nov (week 4). The timeline is ticks with word labels only; no progress fill.\n- Each frame carries a caption strip under it, in 12/16 text.secondary, starting \"Carries:\".\n- Draw no new card style. Callouts are raised surface, radius lg, shadow sm, with text.primary body. The HONESTY tag is a neutral pill in surface.sunken.\n\nFAILURE BRANCHES (each drawn, with its recovery and the surface it lands on)\n- B1 · Jordan taps Skip. Starts at F02 (the 44pt Skip on the row) or at F03 (Skip in the sheet); draw both arrows. Skip is stored on the server. It lands on f11-keeper-naming · ios · 08-skipped-landing and f11-keeper-strip · ios · 08-skipped, drawn with R13's B1 host (R2 with the invitation removed and slot 4b at zero height; no keeper anywhere): the slot is closed, Today matches a Today with no keeper, and InlineUndo reads \"Skipped. You can add a keeper from your place file. · Undo\". Next, R9 (Today on Fri 23 Oct, 7:30 AM), captioned \"never asks again\". The way back: R10, the place file with the Place section row \"Give this place a keeper · Add\", then f11-keeper-naming · ios · 14-reentry with the PLACE B title, the single scope line and no Skip. Save returns to the row, which reads \"Pepper · Red fox\" and announces \"Pepper is on Today now.\" Settings › \"Keeper\" is the second way back. Rejoins at F06 on the next Today open. Callout: \"The exported 'Skipped' frame in v1 kept the invitation. This must not ship.\"\n- B2 · The invitation window ends without a tap. Starts at F01. R11 (Today on Sun 1 Nov): the slot closed silently after Fri 30 Oct, with no Undo and no message. The place file row \"Give this place a keeper · Add\" (as in R10) remains the way back. Ends here.\n- B3 · Save fails. Starts at F05. f11-keeper-naming · ios · 06-save-error with R13's B3 host (R2 behind the scrim, invitation still at 4b) and sheet swaps: InlineErrorRow \"We couldn't save that. Your name is still here.\", \"Retry saving\", and \"Pepper\" kept. Rejoins at F05.\n- B4 · Offline at naming. Starts at F03. f11-keeper-naming · ios · 13-offline with R13's B4 host (R2 behind the scrim, invitation still at 4b) and sheet swaps: \"Name the keeper\" disabled with \"You're offline. You can name it when you're back.\" Skip still works and shows \"Will save when you're back online\". Rejoins at F02 when the connection returns (the invitation is still there), or at B1 if he skipped.\n- B5 · An air alert is on screen (flow-10, alert variant AQI 118, Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups, 4:00 PM, at Jordan's saved place). Starts at F06. R12, dated Tue 27 Oct, 4:10 PM (an illustrative date; list it on Notes): the AqiBand alert owns the screen, the keeper slot collapses to zero height, and no avatar or mood appears anywhere. Rejoins at F06 when the alert clears.\n- B6 · Offline on Today. Starts at F06. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 16-offline with R13's B6 host (R5) and keeper swaps: \"On it · as of 7:41 AM\" (the export's \"as of 7:04 AM\" predates Pepper's naming), the line \"Garbage tomorrow.\" kept, the avatar desaturated, FactCount, keeper strip variant in its offline state, and the name menu items disabled with \"You're offline. You can change the keeper when you're back.\" Rejoins at F06 when the connection returns.\n- B7 · Hide or remove. Starts at F06. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 09-menu-open (Rename · Change species · Hide keeper for now · Remove keeper), with R13's B7 host (R5) and keeper swaps. The hide path is ios · 10-hide-choice with the PLACE B dates: \"Hide for 7 days · until Wed 28 Oct\", \"Hide for 31 days · until Sat 21 Nov\", then \"Keeper hidden until Wed 28 Oct · Undo\", with \"Show keeper now\" in the place file. The remove path is ios · 11-removed-undo with the PLACE B string \"Keeper removed · Undo\": it happens at once, with no dialog and no creature emotion. After Remove, the place file row reads \"Give this place a keeper · Add\" (R10). Hide rejoins at a Today like R5 with slot 4b at zero height and no invitation (the invitation never returns after a hide) until Wed 28 Oct, then at R5 again. Remove ends at R10 with \"Give this place a keeper · Add\".\n- B8 · Jordan later claims the address (flow-06). Starts at F06. R14, the recast claim receipt (Wed 28 Oct, 6:10 PM, illustrative). Then R16, the claimed Today: \"Pepper · Busy\" / \"3 things due in the next 7 days.\", ScopeChip \"Your household\", the notice \"Birchfield Ct is now your home · See what moved\", and FactCount, keeper strip variant [export label \"V2\"], \"5 on file\" with Place · Dates, now without the T1 limit; the address reads 1107 NE Birchfield Ct. Callout: \"After the claim, FactCount leaves the T1 rule [V3] for the household keeper strip [V2]: Money, People and Proof pips can now appear once something is on file; the count stays 5 today. Property tax becomes a mood input at a claimed home, so the mood is Busy.\" If the naming sheet is opened after the claim, its scope lines read \"Everyone in this household will see this.\" and \"What it says is based on what each person can see.\" Ends on the claimed Today (R16).\n- B9 · A member without rename rights. Jordan has no household, so draw this at HOME A. f11-keeper-strip · ios · 12-member-view: Sam's menu with \"Hide keeper for now\" and the disabled \"Rename or change · only Maya\", with the footer \"Only Maya can rename this keeper.\" and no Remove item. Then f11-keeper-naming · ios · 10-member-read-only: \"Ollie, this place's keeper\", \"Maya named this place's keeper Ollie.\" and the LockedActionRow. Callout: \"flow-spec's 'Only Sam can rename' becomes 'Only Maya can rename this keeper.': Maya is the owner.\" Ends here.\n- B10 · Must never ship. Draw the three R15 specimens, each crossed out with a diagonal \"MUST NOT SHIP\" band and a one-line reason: (a) R1 with the naming sheet auto-presented over it, labelled \"design doc §F11: auto-present on the second Today open\"; (b) the lock-screen notification \"Pepper misses you\", labelled \"the keeper never sends a push\"; (c) the strip with a streak chip and \"Pepper knows 5 things\", labelled \"no streaks, no promotions, never 'knows'\". Ends here.\n\nHANDOFF CHECKS (draw each as a pair of cropped thumbnails with a check line and a PASS or MISMATCH word label; these come from the flows-spec handoff gaps and the export review. [10] and [11] name the artboard each check sits on.)\n- [10] F01, F02 and the design doc §F11 must agree that nothing opens without a tap. The sheet opens only from the invitation row, the strip menu, the place file row or Settings.\n- [10] F03 and B1 must agree on what Skip does: the slot closes for good, with no leftover invitation. The v1 f11-keeper-naming \"Skipped\" frame kept it.\n- [10] F03, F04, the pose sheet (f11-keeper-strip · ios · 23-pose-sheet) and the claim receipt (B8) must use one species list: Octopus, River otter, Great blue heron, Red fox, Raccoon, Douglas squirrel. Jordan's keeper is \"Pepper · Red fox\" everywhere. The design doc (otter, owl, fox, heron, cat, dog), flow-spec (Octopus → Ollie) and the claim receipt export (\"Ollie · Otter\") are superseded.\n- [10] F03, R4 and B8 must use the right scope block: one line, \"Only you will see this.\", at a saved place, and two lines (\"Everyone in this household will see this.\" and \"What it says is based on what each person can see.\") only after the claim. MISMATCH if a PLACE B export shows the second line.\n- [10] F01 and F03 must use the two scope forms: the sheet says \"Only you will see this.\", and Today's chip says \"Saved place · Only you\". Never \"Only you see this.\".\n- [10] F02 and F06 must put the keeper slot in one place: 4b, after the 14-day card and before the weather, in both f1-today-tab and f11-keeper-strip.\n- [10] F02, B1 and the place file must use one invitation title at PLACE B: \"Give this place a keeper\". The x-place-file specimen \"Give your place a keeper · Add\" becomes \"Give this place a keeper · Add\" at a saved place.\n- [10] F05 and F06 must use one confirmation: \"Pepper is on Today now.\" as the caption under the strip and as the status message.\n- [10] B1, B3, B4 and F06 must agree on when a keeper exists: the Skip landing and the naming-sheet branches show no strip and no Pepper behind them (host R2); only B6 and B7 use the named host (R5). PASS once R13's host split is drawn.\n- [11] F06 and F07 must show the same count: \"5 on file\", with the pips Place · Dates, by the x-place-file rule. The exports disagree: f11-keeper-strip says \"7 on file\", x-place-file says \"2 on file\" (before Jordan's dates), f1-claim-receipt says \"11 on file\", and flow-spec says \"6 on file\". MISMATCH also at the source of f11-keeper-strip's number: it takes \"7 on file\" from Foundations 00b-07 (the FactCount T1 specimen), so the Foundations 00b board must change to 5 as well. The design doc's \"knows 6 things\" is retired. B8 adds a note: the receipt's \"2 dates\" and the place file's 3 date rows differ only because the notice deadline is a caption on the receipt.\n- [11] F06, B6 and B8 must use the contract's FactCount variant names (keeper strip, place file header, T1), with the export labels V2 and V3 in brackets.\n- [11] F02 and F06 must use one wording for tomorrow's pickup at PLACE B. The PickupCard headline is \"Garbage tomorrow\", while the f11-keeper-strip export says \"Pickup tomorrow.\" and flow-spec says \"Recycling tomorrow.\" The storyboard draws \"Garbage tomorrow.\" on the strip; the founder confirms. The caveat is carried once by the PickupCard, and the strip carries only the wordless hollow mark.\n- [11] F06 and F07 must agree on what T1 can hold. The strip draws no outline for Money, People or Proof, and the place file shows those categories only as the grey row \"Money, people and proof · Not here — this is a saved place · Claim this address first\". Neither frame shows a ring or a fraction.\n- [11] F01 and F07 must agree on the first-week state. No \"3 of 6 things on file →\" progress row appears on Today, the FirstWeekRow is gone from Sat 17 Oct (the first week is Sat 10 to Fri 16 Oct, the same window as §5 activation), and the place file shows no \"Set up your place\" block; the still-undone pickup step appears only as the standalone \"Next for this place\" row. f1-today-tab and x-place-file date Jordan's save Sat 17 Oct; the storyboard uses the fixture date, Sat 10 Oct.\n- [11] F02 (R2) and the 14-day card export must agree on the window: on Wed 21 Oct the window runs to Tue 3 Nov, so property tax (Mon 2 Nov) and the Tue 3 Nov statewide bar join the card (\"Next 14 days: 6 items\"), as in R9, R11 and R12. The export (Mon 19 Oct) shows 4 items. PASS once R2 lists every row.\n- [11] F08, F09 and the property-tax signal must agree on mood inputs at a saved place. The storyboard treats seeded property tax as a county signal, not a PLACE B mood input, so F08 stays Calm with property tax due Mon 2 Nov inside the window. MISMATCH: f11-keeper-strip lists \"seeded property tax\" as a mood input with no saved-place exception; f1-today-tab shows the property-tax signal at PLACE B while x-place-file says \"County dates aren't available for a saved place\". The founder confirms the rule, and f11-keeper-strip and f1-today-tab (or x-place-file) change to match.\n- [11] F08, the F09 inset and the Calm string must not contradict what is on screen. MISMATCH (Honesty): the export line \"No bills or dates due in the next 7 days.\" claims no dates while \"Pay property tax, 2nd half · in 2 days · due Mon 2 Nov\" (F08) or \"Today · due Mon 2 Nov\" (F09 inset) is drawn below it and the Tue 3 Nov voting day is in the window; it also mentions bills, which a T1 place cannot hold. The house-style Honesty rule allows an all-clear only when it is true. The storyboard draws the proposal \"Nothing of yours due in the next 7 days.\" (scoped to Jordan's own items) and shows the export string crossed out. f11-keeper-strip changes its saved-place Calm string; the founder confirms the wording.\n- [11] B6 and the KeeperStrip contract must use one offline mood word. Compare only the word: \"On it\" (the export and the storyboard) vs \"Attentive\" (the contract). MISMATCH; the contract changes. The time after it is Jordan's own (\"as of 7:41 AM\").\n- [11] B8 and F06 must agree on consent. After the claim, the receipt states that everyone in the household will see Pepper (and the pickup day); the strip never announces the scope change itself. MISMATCH against house-style invariant 2 (\"Scope changes need an explicit choice\"): the receipt asks a consent question only for the 2 dates, while the keeper row and the pickup-day row become visible to the household with no choice offered. The founder decides whether a keeper (and a seeded pickup day) needs consent; log it for f1-claim-receipt.\n- [11] F07 (R6, R10) and B8 (R14) must use one relative-count form for far dates. MISMATCH (cross-project): x-place-file says \"in 5 months · Wed 31 Mar 2027\" and \"in 4 months · Mon 1 Mar 2027\", while f1-claim-receipt says \"in 154 days · Wed 31 Mar 2027\" (and x-date-sheet \"in 133 days · Mon 1 Mar 2027\"). The storyboard keeps each export's own form; the founder picks one, and x-place-file or f1-claim-receipt changes.\n- [11] B9 and f11-keeper-naming must name the owner: \"Only Maya can rename this keeper.\"\n\nACCESSIBILITY IN THE JOURNEY (draw as artboard 12: a focus-path strip of 25% thumbnails of each frame, labelled \"thumbnail\", with a numbered focus dot on each)\n- F01: Today is read in visual order: location row, receipt, property-tax heads-up, 14-day card, then the invitation row, read \"Give this place a keeper, button\" followed by \"Skip, button\". Nothing is announced on load.\n- F02 → F03: focus moves to the sheet title \"Give this place a keeper\" and is trapped inside the sheet. Close, Escape and Back return focus to the invitation row and change nothing.\n- F03 → F04: focus stays on the tile, which reads \"Red fox, suggested name Pepper, selected\". The disabled \"Name the keeper\" was focusable and read \"Pick an animal first\".\n- F04 → F05: \"Saving…\" is announced as a status.\n- F05 → F06: the sheet closes. Focus returns to the keeper slot, now the name button \"Pepper, keeper options\", and \"Pepper is on Today now.\" is announced as role=status. The strip label reads \"Pepper, on it: Garbage tomorrow. On record, not confirmed.\"\n- F06 → F07: the count reads \"5 things on file: place, dates. Opens your place file.\" Focus lands on the title \"Your place file\". Back returns focus to the count.\n- F08: the strip reads \"Pepper, calm: Nothing of yours due in the next 7 days.\" (the proposal).\n- F09: \"Couldn't check what's due. Your dates didn't load.\" is announced politely. Retry is labelled \"Retry checking your dates\".\n- B1: after Skip, focus lands on the InlineUndo line, and \"Skipped. You can add a keeper from your place file.\" is announced.\n- The no-notifications path is the whole journey: Jordan never turned notifications on. Every step starts from an organic open from the app icon, and the keeper sends nothing. Draw a small panel stating this, with a crop of Notification settings showing that no keeper group exists, and a note that Jordan's activation came from the widget, not from a briefing.\n- Motion: the pose change is one transition of 300ms or less. Under Reduce Motion, poses are static and transitions cross-fade. Draw a static pair to show this.\n- Greyscale and large text: attach f11-keeper-strip · ios · 22-greyscale, ios · 21-ax5, f11-keeper-naming · ios · 18-ax5 and ios · 19-greyscale, with the captions \"Calm and Unavailable differ by pose and words, not hue\" and \"At AX5 the avatar sits on top and FactCount moves below the line\".\n- Targets: the invitation row, Skip, each tile, the mood line, the count and the name are each 44pt (48dp on Android). The hollow mark is never a target by itself.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of Maya at a saved place (flow-spec's persona), draw Jordan at PLACE B, because Maya's HOME A is a claimed home with a household and cannot show the T1 moment.\n- Instead of Octopus → \"Ollie\" at 5 / 24, draw Red fox → \"Pepper\" at 6 / 24, because Ollie is HOME A's otter and Jordan's exported keeper is Pepper.\n- Instead of a Jordan with no briefing and no widget, give him the widget on Sun 11 Oct, because only an activated user can move the week-four return metric, and the widget keeps notifications off.\n- Instead of auto-presenting the sheet on the second open, show the invitation ignored on F01 and tapped on F02, because someone checking the bins must not be interrupted by a naming ask.\n- Instead of \"6 on file\", \"7 on file\" or \"knows 6 things\", draw \"5 on file\" on both the strip and the place file, because the two numbers must match and follow one rule.\n- Instead of \"Nothing due this week.\" and \"Recycling tomorrow.\", use a rolling 7-day line and \"Garbage tomorrow.\", because the window is rolling and PLACE B's recycling is Not set.\n- Instead of the export Calm line \"No bills or dates due in the next 7 days.\" above a visible property-tax date, draw \"Nothing of yours due in the next 7 days.\" as the proposal and cross out the export string, because an all-clear must be true for everything it names.\n- Instead of \"Couldn't check what's due\" with a calm-looking pose, draw the neutral outline pose and name the failed input, because a quiet face on a failed check is a lie.\n- Instead of leaving the invitation after Skip, close the slot and show the way back in the place file, because a skipped ask should not return.\n- Instead of one named host for every PLACE B branch, use R2 where no keeper exists yet and R5 only where Pepper is named, because a Pepper strip behind a Skip or a failing save is a false break.\n- Instead of carrying Maya's receipt content into Jordan's claim, recast every row of the receipt, because a branch that shows another person's dates is not Jordan's journey.\n- Instead of redrawing any exported screen from memory, place the export and change only the listed deltas, because the storyboard exists to show what breaks between screens, not to redesign them.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- F01 and F02 show that the invitation never interrupts: what's due is read first on both.\n- Naming takes two taps (Red fox, then Name the keeper), and Skip takes one, is stored, can be undone and has a drawn way back.\n- \"5 on file\" is identical on F06 and F07, and every other count in the exports (and the Foundations 00b specimen) is logged as a mismatch.\n- Every mood (On it, Calm, Busy, Unavailable) traces to named records or a named failure, Unavailable never looks like Calm, the property-tax exclusion is stated beside F08, and no Calm line contradicts a date drawn on the same screen.\n- The hollow Thursday mark travels from the PickupCard to the strip without the strip claiming the day is confirmed.\n- Jordan's activation (address, widget, date; activated Tue 13 Oct) is visible on the timeline, the first week has one definition (Sat 10 to Fri 16 Oct), and the week-four annotation is true.\n- Every 14-day card lists every row in its window with relative counts that match its frame's date, and states its summary count.\n- All ten branches are drawn, each with its recovery and the frame it rejoins or ends on, including the three must-not-ship specimens, and every branch redraw (including R16) is on the REDRAW list.\n- Every frame shows its date and time, and the three time jumps are labelled gaps.\n- The focus path, the no-notifications panel, Reduce Motion, greyscale and AX5 are drawn.\n- Android and web appear on the platform-twins artboard for the sheet and the strip, each captioned as a HOME A export.\n- No storyboard frame is scaled below 50%, only labelled thumbnails are at 25%, and nothing overlaps.\n\nARTBOARDS\n1. flow-09 · storyboard · 01-before-the-tap-lane · light — the timeline, F01 (R1), the \"Wed 21 Oct, 7:40 AM\" gap, and F02 (R2), with branch tags.\n2. flow-09 · storyboard · 02-naming-lane · light — F03 (R3), F04, F05 (R4).\n3. flow-09 · storyboard · 03-landing-and-count-lane · light — F06 (R5) and F07 (R6), with the count-match callout.\n4. flow-09 · storyboard · 04-later-days-lane · light — the \"Sat 31 Oct\" gap, F08 (R7) with its window note, Honesty callout and crossed-out export string, the \"Mon 2 Nov\" gap, F09 (R8) with its retry inset, and the week-4 bracket.\n5. flow-09 · storyboard · 05-branches-skip-and-window-lane · light — B1 (with R13's B1 host, R9 and R10), B2 (R11), B3, B4 (with R13's naming-sheet host).\n6. flow-09 · storyboard · 06-branches-context-lane · light — B5 (R12), B6, B7 (with R13's named host).\n7. flow-09 · storyboard · 07-branches-claim-and-member-lane · light — B8 (R14, then R16), B9.\n8. flow-09 · storyboard · 08-must-not-ship-lane · light — B10's three crossed-out specimens (R15).\n9. flow-09 · storyboard · 09-platform-twins-lane · light — the naming sheet on Android, web-1440 and web-390 (from the 15, 16 and 17 exports) and the strip on Android, web-1440 and web-390 (from the 18, 19 and 20 exports). Every twin is a HOME A export, so each caption starts with what the export shows and then gives the PLACE B reading: naming twins \"export shows HOME A (River otter · Ollie picked, two household scope lines); at PLACE B these read: 'Give this place a keeper', 'Red fox · Pepper', 'Only you will see this.'\"; strip twins \"export shows HOME A (Ollie · Busy, a dense household strip); at PLACE B these read: 'Pepper · On it · Garbage tomorrow.', '5 on file' (Place · Dates)\". Each caption ends with the one platform difference it shows (for example \"web 1440: 480-wide modal; FactCount at most 160px\").\n10. flow-09 · storyboard · 10-handoff-checks-naming-lane · light — the checks marked [10], each as a pair of crops with its check line and a PASS or MISMATCH word label (no colour-only status).\n11. flow-09 · storyboard · 11-handoff-checks-count-and-mood-lane · light — the checks marked [11], drawn the same way.\n12. flow-09 · storyboard · 12-accessibility-lane · light — the focus path, the announcements, the no-notifications panel, the Reduce Motion pair, and the greyscale and AX5 references.\n13. flow-09 · Notes — The recast (flow-spec's Maya Chen, 34, T1, week 3, at 7:40 AM becomes Jordan Lee at PLACE B). The fixture save date Sat 10 Oct, overriding the Sat 17 Oct used in f1-today-tab and x-place-file. One first-week definition: Sat 10 to Fri 16 Oct, used for both §5 activation and the FirstWeekRow; the invitation is eligible from Sat 17 Oct and its 14-day window runs through Fri 30 Oct. Export re-datings: f11-keeper-strip 13-saved-place from Wed 21 Oct, 6:10 PM to 7:41 AM; 05-calm from Wed 21 Oct (HOME A) to Sat 31 Oct (PLACE B); 06-unavailable to Mon 2 Nov (PLACE B); x-place-file 02 moved past its first week; f5-today-calendar-strip 03 re-dated to Wed 21 Oct with its window extended to Tue 3 Nov; f1-today-tab 13-after-claim re-dated to Wed 28 Oct with the keeper strip added at 4b (R16). R13's host split: B1 on R2 with slot 4b closed; B3 and B4 on R2 behind the scrim with the invitation; B6 and B7 on R5. Invented facts and strings: the widget added Sun 11 Oct (Jordan's activation); the renters-insurance date added Tue 13 Oct (activation date); the lease saved Mon 19 Oct at 6:08 PM; the Sun 18 Oct first invitation visit; \"Pepper is on Today now.\"; \"Couldn't check what's due. Your dates didn't load.\"; \"Retry checking your dates\"; \"Nothing of yours due in the next 7 days.\" (the proposed saved-place Calm string; the export string \"No bills or dates due in the next 7 days.\" is shown crossed out); \"Hide for 7 days · until Wed 28 Oct\"; \"Hide for 31 days · until Sat 21 Nov\"; \"Keeper hidden until Wed 28 Oct · Undo\"; \"Give this place a keeper · Add\"; \"Pepper (your keeper) · Red fox\"; \"Your pickup day, 2 dates and Pepper came with you.\"; \"Address confirmed by postcard · Wed 28 Oct\"; the Wed 28 Oct, 6:10 PM claim date (flow-06 owns the real one); R16's \"Pepper · Busy\" / \"3 things due in the next 7 days.\" and its inputs (pickup Thu 29 Oct, renters insurance Fri 30 Oct, property tax Mon 2 Nov) and the holding-papers pose; \"On it · as of 7:41 AM\" (replacing the export's 7:04 AM); \"Checked 7:45 AM · weather · air · alerts · your calendar\" and \"Checked 7:15 AM · …\"; the Tue 27 Oct, 4:10 PM alert date; the 14-day rows and summaries on R2 (6 items: \"Tomorrow · Thu 22 Oct\", \"in 5 days · must arrive by Mon 26 Oct\", \"in 8 days · Thu 29 Oct\", \"in 9 days · Fri 30 Oct\", \"in 12 days · due Mon 2 Nov\", the Tue 3 Nov bar \"in 13 days\", week-two label \"Wed 28\"), R9 (6 items), R11 (4 items) and R12 (5 items); the relative counts on R2, R6, R8 (\"Today · due Mon 2 Nov\"), R10 and R14, including the place file's month forms \"in 4 months\" and \"in 5 months\" and the receipt's \"in 154 days\"; the strip labels \"Pepper, on it: Garbage tomorrow. On record, not confirmed.\" and \"Pepper, calm: Nothing of yours due in the next 7 days.\"; the must-not-ship specimen strings (\"Pepper misses you\", \"3-day streak\", \"Pepper knows 5 things\"), which are marked as forbidden; the twin captions; the arrow and gap labels. Decisions to confirm: \"Garbage tomorrow.\" on the PLACE B strip; the saved-place Calm string (proposal \"Nothing of yours due in the next 7 days.\"); the \"5 on file\" count (address, Thursday seed, renters insurance, lease ends, notice deadline); the rule that county and state rules (property tax, in-person voting) are shown but excluded from mood and not counted at a saved place, to confirm against the KeeperStrip contract; whether a county heads-up due tomorrow (R11) should cancel the all-clear; the receipt's 2-dates rule vs the place file's 3 date rows; whether the keeper row (and the pickup-day row) on the claim receipt needs an explicit consent choice under house-style invariant 2; one relative-count form for far dates (months in x-place-file vs days in f1-claim-receipt and x-date-sheet); the FactCount variant names (contract names with export labels V2 and V3). Proposed instrumentation: keeper_named, keeper_skipped and keeper_removed as FunnelEvent types, to read the removal and skip rates against week-four return among activated users. Each MISMATCH from artboards 10 and 11, with the project that must change: f11-keeper-strip count, pickup line, saved-place Calm string, mood inputs and HOME A offline time; Foundations 00b (the FactCount T1 specimen \"7 on file\" must change to 5); f11-keeper-naming PLACE B scope block; x-place-file PLACE B title, first-week dates and far-date form (or f1-claim-receipt); f1-today-tab PLACE B property-tax signal and save date; f1-claim-receipt keeper species, name, PLACE B content and the keeper scope-change consent; the KeeperStrip contract's \"Attentive\"; design doc §F11. Omitted states.\n\nBATCH PLAN\nTurn 1: artboards 1-6, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 2: artboards 7-12, then wait for \"continue\".\nTurn 3: artboard 13."
